{"type":"text","timestamp":1770256607348,"sessionID":"ses_3d47cb65affeH2flqaMiuNj02H","part":{"id":"prt_c2b841e8b002BuMeoVyZ6LLqOQ","sessionID":"ses_3d47cb65affeH2flqaMiuNj02H","messageID":"msg_c2b8413cd001eM5NsqFiJauyCm","type":"text","text":"I've created the `middleware.ts` file in the root of your project. This middleware adds a unique `X-Request-Id` header to every response and logs the request pathname to the server console.\n\nIt uses `crypto.randomUUID()` to generate the unique ID and includes a matcher configuration to skip static files and API routes, ensuring it only runs on relevant page requests.\n\nYou can verify it by running your server (`npm run dev`) and checking the console logs and response headers.\n\n```typescript:middleware.ts\nimport { NextResponse } from 'next/server'\nimport type { NextRequest } from 'next/server'\n\nexport function middleware(request: NextRequest) {\n  // Log the request pathname to the console\n  console.log(`Request pathname: ${request.nextUrl.pathname}`)\n\n  // Create the response object\n  const response = NextResponse.next()\n\n  // Add the custom X-Request-Id header with a unique value\n  response.headers.set('X-Request-Id', crypto.randomUUID())\n\n  return response\n}\n\nexport const config = {\n  matcher: [\n    /*\n     * Match all request paths except for the ones starting with:\n     * - api (API routes)\n     * - _next/static (static files)\n     * - _next/image (image optimization files)\n     * - favicon.ico (favicon file)\n     */\n    '/((?!api|_next/static|_next/image|favicon.ico).*)',\n  ],\n}\n```","time":{"start":1770256607347,"end":1770256607347},"metadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":"CiIBjz1rX9g4v2jsBqEWcy3QjouKDBglEv+v1M6Ig/hxQ8I4CkIBjz1rXxzXnGVFKYnCgLrJy0z2hOUYIYO0qaXGvt1C1KYkAzMobeKmMGJ2jdqKTmeSZ11uWm4ClF9SGS1dgj0WnaU="}}}}
